   "title": "Coast Guard drives away foreign fishing vessel off Lawak Island",
   "url": "https://www.inquirer.net/493750/coast-guard-drives-away-foreign-fishing-vessel-off-lawak-island/",
   "domain": "inquirer.net",
   "source": "inquirer.net",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:38:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792791480.0,
   "ageDays": 0.0,
   "summary": "READ: PCG fends off Chinese vessel, 4 small boats off Lawak Island in Palawan The vessel eventually steered northward away from the island, while the PCG team escorted it from a safe distance. In less than four weeks, the PCG recorded six incidents within the KIG, including China’s fishing vessel YUETAIYU 63168 and four small boats off Lawak Island in Oct. 18 and a foreign fishing vessel off Kota Island three days later.",
   "summary_zh": "阅读：菲律宾海岸警卫队驱离中国船只，并在巴拉望岛Lawak岛附近驱离4艘小船。该船最终向北驶离岛屿，菲律宾海岸警卫队随后在安全距离外护送其离开。不到4周内，菲律宾海岸警卫队在KIG海域记录了6起事件，包括中国渔船YUETAIYU 63168，以及10月18日在Lawak岛附近出现的4艘小船和3天后在Kota岛附近出现的一艘外国渔船。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The vessel’s position was monitored 2 nautical miles (nm) northeast of Lawak Island, which is well within its 12-nm territorial sea, the PCG stressed. Upon sighting the foreign ship, PCG personnel were deployed aboard a rubber boat to conduct maritime patrol. They issued repeated radio challenges and warnings to direct them to leave the island’s territorial waters. READ: PCG fends off Chinese vessel, 4 small boats off Lawak Island in Palawan The vessel eventually steered northward away from the island, while the PCG team escorted it from a safe distance. There were no untoward incidents throughout the operation, the PCG said. Lawak Island is part of the municipality of Kalayaan in Palawan province. “Under international law, the Philippines exercises full sovereignty over its territorial sea, where no foreign vessel may fish without authorization,” it stressed. It added that the act is likewise in violation of Philippine laws, including the Philippine Fisheries Code and the Philippine Maritime Zones Act. In less than four weeks, the PCG recorded six incidents within the KIG, including China’s fishing vessel YUETAIYU 63168 and four small boats off Lawak Island in Oct. 18 and a foreign fishing vessel off Kota Island three days later. It also repelled five foreign fishing vessels within the territorial waters of Kota Island last Oct. 11. Your subscription could not be saved. Please try again. Your subscription has been successful. Meanwhile, the PCG also reported that Chinese Maritime Militia Vessel 9622 and its sampans were also chased off after being anchored off Kota Island in Sept. 28 and Oct. 9. /gsg For comprehensive coverage, in-depth analysis, visit our special page for West Philippine Sea updates . Stay informed with articles, videos, and expert opinions",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
