   "_dt": 1792765940.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Ms. Karthika who, was granted bail on Thursday night by the Judicial Magistrate Court in Dharapuram, and released on Friday morning along with eight other party members including her husband Muruga Chandrakumar, was accorded a rousing welcome by NTK party cadre. Unemployment rate was the highest in Tamil Nadu, Ms. Karthika claimed, demanding resignation of the TVK government.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁 Karthika女士周四晚在Dharapuram司法治安法庭获准保释，并于周五上午与包括其丈夫Muruga Chandrakumar在内的另外8名党内人士一同获释；她受到NTK党骨干的热烈欢迎。Karthika女士称，泰米尔纳德邦失业率最高，并要求TVK政府辞职。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Ms. Karthika who, was granted bail on Thursday night by the Judicial Magistrate Court in Dharapuram, and released on Friday morning along with eight other party members including her husband Muruga Chandrakumar, was accorded a rousing welcome by NTK party cadre. Inflation and soaring costs of essential commodities was pushing many into poverty. Chief Minister C. Joseph Vijay has failed to secure the Cauvery water from Karnataka and Palar water from Andhra Pradesh. Unemployment rate was the highest in Tamil Nadu, Ms. Karthika claimed, demanding resignation of the TVK government. The police department, she sought to explain, had acted in an ‘undemocratic’ way by blocking her from electioneering on the final day of campaign on October 4 in Dharapuram, questioning the purported justification behind obstructing all other candidates from seeking votes, in view of the Chief Minister’s roadshow. “The obstruction was unwarranted. We would have completed our campaign at the particular spot within two minutes, and cleared the way,” she pointed out. “I thank the Chief Minister for jailing me for fighting for people’s cause. I am not corrupt. Nor am I involved in trafficking of meth,” she said. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
