   "_dt": 1792765923.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The delinquency ratio on loans extended by banks rose for the second consecutive month in August, data showed Friday. The delinquency numbers on banks' won-denominated loans stood at 0.69 percent as of end-August, up 0.06 percentage point from a month earlier, according to the data from the Financial Supervisory Service (FSS). The amount of newly overdue loans came to 3 trillion won ($2.26 billion) in August, down 0.2 trillion won from the previous month.",
   "summary_zh": "数据显示，银行发放贷款的拖欠率在8月连续第二个月上升。根据金融监督服务局（FSS）的数据，截至8月底，银行以韩元计价贷款的拖欠率为0.69%，较上月上升0.06个百分点。8月新逾期贷款金额为3万亿韩元（22.6亿美元），较上月减少0.2万亿韩元。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The delinquency ratio on loans extended by banks rose for the second consecutive month in August, data showed Friday. The delinquency numbers on banks' won-denominated loans stood at 0.69 percent as of end-August, up 0.06 percentage point from a month earlier, according to the data from the Financial Supervisory Service (FSS). The amount of newly overdue loans came to 3 trillion won ($2.26 billion) in August, down 0.2 trillion won from the previous month. The amount of write-offs of such loans, on the other hand, came in at 1.5 trillion won, up 0.1 trillion won over the cited period, according to the FSS. The delinquency ratio for corporate loans stood at 0.86 percent as of end-August, up 0.08 percentage point from a month earlier, and the ratio for household loans rose 0.03 percentage point to 0.45 percent over the same period",
