   "title": "‘Suspension orders’ issued for 106 medical shops over sale of habit forming drugs",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/suspension-orders-issued-for-106-medical-shops-over-sale-of-habit-forming-drugs/article71616485.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:01:31 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792765891.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Telangana Standards Authority for Food and Essential Drugs (TG SAFE) has suspended 106 medical shops in Hyderabad and its surrounding areas for violations relating to the sale of habit-forming drugs, while cancelling one licence, and issuing warnings to three establishments.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后解锁。Telangana Standards Authority for Food and Essential Drugs（TG SAFE）已暂停海得拉巴及周边地区106家药店的经营执照，原因是这些药店涉及销售会成瘾的药品；此外，该机构还吊销了1张执照，并向3家机构发出警告。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Telangana Standards Authority for Food and Essential Drugs (TG SAFE) has suspended 106 medical shops in Hyderabad and its surrounding areas for violations relating to the sale of habit-forming drugs, while cancelling one licence, and issuing warnings to three establishments. The action follows a special enforcement drive conducted by the Drugs Wing of TG SAFE where raids were carried out at medical shops in vulnerable areas to curb the illegal sale and diversion of habit-forming drugs. A total of 110 actions were initiated against medical shops found violating provisions of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940, and the rules framed under it. Of the 106 suspension orders issued, 99 shops have been suspended until further orders, while two establishments face suspension for three days, and five for seven days. One drug licence has been cancelled, and three establishments have been issued warnings. TG SAFE has cautioned chemists and druggists against selling habit-forming drugs, including psychotropic medicines and Schedule H and H1 drugs, without valid prescriptions from registered medical practitioners. It has also directed medical shops to maintain purchase, sale and stock records as required under the law. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
