   "ageDays": 0.17,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Mysuru is among 17 cities across the country selected to establish dedicated street food hubs under the Pradhan Mantri Street Vendor’s AtmaNirbhar Nidhi (PM SVANidhi) scheme, an initiative aimed at supporting street vendors while promoting local cuisine and tourism. The initiative of the Union Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs (MoHUA) seeks to provide organised spaces for street food vendors, improve food safety and hygiene, and offer better facilities to customers.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁这些内容。迈索鲁是全国入选的17个城市之一，将根据“总理街头摊贩自立基金”（PM SVANidhi）计划设立专门的街头食品中心。该计划旨在支持街头摊贩，同时推广当地美食和旅游。印度联邦住房和城市事务部（MoHUA）的这项计划 seeks 为街头食品摊贩提供规范化经营空间，改善食品安全和卫生，并为顾客提供更好的设施。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Mysuru is among 17 cities across the country selected to establish dedicated street food hubs under the Pradhan Mantri Street Vendor’s AtmaNirbhar Nidhi (PM SVANidhi) scheme, an initiative aimed at supporting street vendors while promoting local cuisine and tourism. The initiative of the Union Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs (MoHUA) seeks to provide organised spaces for street food vendors, improve food safety and hygiene, and offer better facilities to customers. The proposed hub in Mysuru is expected to provide food stalls, seating, drinking water, toilets, adequate lighting, signboards, solid waste management facilities, and digital payment options, along with arrangements to ensure compliance with food safety standards. The facility is expected to improve the vending environment, help vendors enhance their earnings, and offer tourists a better experience of Mysuru’s local cuisine, according the Mysuru City Corporation (MCC). Mysuru’s selection is significant given its rich culinary heritage, tourism potential, and reputation as a clean city. The project is expected to support local food businesses while adding to the city’s tourism attractions. The initiative aligns with broader efforts to improve urban amenities, promote cleanliness, and strengthen the livelihood of street vendors. The hub is expected to provide an opportunity to showcase Mysuru’s traditional food and culinary culture to a wider audience while creating a more organised and hygienic environment for vendors and visitors, said MCC Commissioner M. K. Savita. The project is part of the government’s efforts to promote inclusive urban development and improve livelihood opportunities for street vendors under the PM SVANidhi framework. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
