   "title": "919203 akwa ibom assembly adopts recommendations to establish state police",
   "url": "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/regional/south-south-regional/919203-akwa-ibom-assembly-adopts-recommendations-to-establish-state-police.html",
   "domain": "premiumtimesng.com",
   "source": "Premium Times（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:13:02 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792667582.0,
   "ageDays": 1.16,
   "summary": "The Akwa Ibom House of Assembly has approved the recommendations of its committee on Inter-Governmental, Political and Special Matters to support the proposed establishment of state police in Nigeria. The Speaker, Udeme Otong said the bill sought to establish a constitutional framework for state police services. Mr Otong said the proposed framework would promote cooperation between federal and state police services through information sharing and mutual assistance.",
   "summary_zh": "阿夸伊博姆州议会已批准其政府间事务、政治事务和特别事务委员会的建议，支持在尼日利亚设立州警察的提案。议长Udeme Otong表示，该法案旨在为州警察服务建立宪法框架。Otong先生表示，拟议框架将通过信息共享和相互协助，促进联邦与州警察服务之间的合作。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Akwa Ibom House of Assembly has approved the recommendations of its committee on Inter-Governmental, Political and Special Matters to support the proposed establishment of state police in Nigeria. The approval followed a unanimous vote by the assembly members during the sitting on Wednesday. Presenting the report, the committee Chairman, Emem Udom, said the committee had examined the provisions of the National Policing Bill, and recommended its approval without amendment. The Speaker, Udeme Otong said the bill sought to establish a constitutional framework for state police services. “It also sought to retain the federal police service and its responsibilities for federal policing functions,” he said. Mr Otong said the proposed framework would promote cooperation between federal and state police services through information sharing and mutual assistance. The speaker said that state police would bring policing closer to the people, improve responses to security threats and enhance crime prevention through local intelligence and community engagement. He further said that establishing state police services would create employment opportunities for the youth. In another development, the assembly commended President Bola Tinubu for establishing the Federal University of Agriculture and Technology, Obio Akpa, in Oruk Anam Local Government Area of the state. The commendation followed a motion by the Deputy Whip, Bernard Idiong, which Eric Akpan supported",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
