   "summary": "The Korean won extended its gains to hit a fresh two-year high against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, supported by strong exports and foreign inflows. The won was quoted at 1,325.2 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., up 2.9 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. Earlier in the day, government data showed that the nation's exports more than doubled to US$61.6 billion in the first 20 days of October, driven by robust shipments of semiconductor.",
   "summary_zh": "韩元延续涨势，周三兑美元汇率创下两年新高，强劲出口和外资流入为其提供支撑。下午3时30分，韩元汇率报1美元兑1325.2韩元，较前一交易日收盘价上涨2.9韩元。当天早些时候，政府数据显示，该国10月前20天出口额翻番以上，达到616亿美元，主要受半导体出货量强劲驱动。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Korean won extended its gains to hit a fresh two-year high against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, supported by strong exports and foreign inflows. The won was quoted at 1,325.2 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., up 2.9 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. For a fourth straight session, the won marked the highest level since Oct. 2, 2024. Earlier in the day, government data showed that the nation's exports more than doubled to US$61.6 billion in the first 20 days of October, driven by robust shipments of semiconductor. Foreign purchased a net 659.9 billion won ($497.3 million) worth of local shares during the latest regular stock trading session, with the benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index gaining 3.29 percent to close at 5,735.66",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
