   "title": "Fintiri Tasks Council Chairmen on Anti-Corruption, Procurement Fraud",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/fintiri-tasks-council-chairmen-on-anti-corruption-procurement-fraud/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:03:37 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792551817.0,
   "ageDays": 2.5,
   "summary": "The governor stated this while declaring open a capacity-building training on anti-corruption and procurement fraud organised by the Adamawa State Government in partnership with MDKODM Global Limited at the Banquet Hall of Government House, Yola.",
   "summary_zh": "州长在宣布由阿达马瓦州政府与MDKODM环球有限公司合作在约拉政府大楼宴会厅举办的反腐败和采购欺诈能力建设培训班开幕时发表了上述讲话。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The governor stated this while declaring open a capacity-building training on anti-corruption and procurement fraud organised by the Adamawa State Government in partnership with MDKODM Global Limited at the Banquet Hall of Government House, Yola. The training, organised for the 21 local government council chairmen and relevant officials, is aimed at equipping participants with the knowledge and skills to identify, prevent and address corrupt practices, strengthen accountability and improve service delivery at the grassroots. Represented by the Chief of Staff, Government House, Yola, the governor described the training as timely and relevant, particularly as his administration pursues reforms to improve governance and deliver tangible benefits to the people of the state. Fintiri said corruption undermines public confidence, weakens institutions, increases the cost of governance and deprives citizens of essential services. He noted that local government councils were closest to the people and had direct responsibility for providing basic services, stressing the need to ensure that public funds allocated for development were managed responsibly and used for their intended purposes. The governor also identified procurement as a critical area requiring sustained attention in public financial management. “I expect chairmen of local governments, directors of finance, procurement officers, treasurers, internal auditors and other relevant officials to take the lessons from this training seriously and translate them into practical improvements in their respective offices,” he said. Earlier, the Commissioner for Local Government and Chieftaincy Affairs, Alhaji Ibrahim Yayaji Mijinyawa, described the training as a strategic intervention designed to strengthen internal controls, equip public officers with the necessary skills and institutionalise transparency in line with global best practices and public procurement laws. Mijinyawa said the Fintiri administration maintained a zero-tolerance policy for corruption, adding that the training was intended to ensure that ignorance was not used as an excuse for malpractice. Also speaking, one of the lead consultants and facilitators, Kazeem Atitebi, said the governor had a vision for the state and urged local government chairmen and their officials to align their activities with the administration’s objectives. Atitebi said the training would emphasise integrity, accountability and the efficient use of resources allocated to local government councils. He added that participants would be sensitised to the meaning, forms and causes of corruption in public service, while the programme would promote ethical conduct, honesty and integrity in the discharge of official responsibilities. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "芬蒂里要求市政委员会主席打击腐败和采购欺诈",
   "body_zh": "州长在宣布由阿达马瓦州政府与MDKODM Global Limited合作在约拉政府大楼宴会厅举办的反腐败和采购欺诈能力建设培训时发表了上述讲话。这次培训是为21个地方政府委员会主席和相关官员组织的，旨在为参与者提供知识和技能，以识别、预防和处理腐败行为，加强问责制并改善基层服务交付。由约拉政府大楼办公室主任代表出席的州长称此次培训非常及时且切合实际，特别是因为他的政府正在推行改革以改善治理并为该州人民带来切实利益。芬蒂里表示，腐败会削弱公众信心、削弱机构、增加治理成本并剥夺公民的基本服务。他指出，地方政府委员会最接近民众，并直接负责提供基本服务，强调有必要确保分配用于发展的公共资金得到负责任的管理并用于其预定目的。州长还指出采购是公共财务管理中需要持续关注的关键领域。“我期望地方政府主席、财务主任、采购官员、财务主管、内部审计员和其他相关官员认真对待本次培训的课程，并将其转化为各自办公室的实际改进，”他说。此前，地方政府和酋长事务专员阿尔哈吉·易卜拉欣·雅亚吉·米吉尼亚瓦称此次培训是一项战略干预措施，旨在加强内部控制、为公职人员提供必要技能，并按照全球最佳做法和公共采购法将透明度制度化。米吉尼亚瓦说，芬蒂里政府对腐败实行零容忍政策，并补充说此次培训旨在确保不会以无知作为不当行为的借口。在发言中，其中一位首席顾问和培训师卡泽姆·阿蒂特比表示，州长对该州有愿景，并敦促地方政府主席及其官员将其活动与政府的目标保持一致。阿蒂特比说，此次培训将强调诚信、问责制以及对分配给地方政府委员会资源的有效利用。他补充说，参与者将了解公共服务中腐败的含义、形式和原因，而该计划将促进在履行官方职责时遵守道德行为、诚实和正直。我们拥有优势。获取实时报道、突发独家新闻和独家视角，直接发送到您的手机。不要满足于过时新闻。加入LEADERSHIP NEWS的WhatsApp，获取24/7更新→",
