   "snippet": "An insightful exchange with Ambassador Roh Jae-heon of the Republic of #Korea to #China following his lecture on “The Future of China–ROK Relations.”\n\nDrawing on my visits to South Korea, including filming a documentary about the Demilitarized Zone, I asked about opportunities for China and South Korea to strengthen transport connectivity with Central Asia and extend cooperation towards Europe through the Middle Corridor, including #Azerbaijan and the South Caucasus.\n\nIn response, the Ambassador explained that the absence of direct overland connectivity through North Korea gives particular importance to cooperation with China as a gateway to Central Asia and, further west, the South Caucasus.\n\nFor Azerbaijan, this opens up an important discussion on the Middle Corridor’s potential to connect not only China, but also South Korea, with Europe. 🇦🇿🇰🇷🇨🇳",
   "body": "An insightful exchange with Ambassador Roh Jae-heon of the Republic of #Korea to #China following his lecture on “The Future of China–ROK Relations.”\n\nDrawing on my visits to South Korea, including filming a documentary about the Demilitarized Zone, I asked about opportunities for China and South Korea to strengthen transport connectivity with Central Asia and extend cooperation towards Europe through the Middle Corridor, including #Azerbaijan and the South Caucasus.\n\nIn response, the Ambassador explained that the absence of direct overland connectivity through North Korea gives particular importance to cooperation with China as a gateway to Central Asia and, further west, the South Caucasus.\n\nFor Azerbaijan, this opens up an important discussion on the Middle Corridor’s potential to connect not only China, but also South Korea, with Europe. 🇦🇿🇰🇷🇨🇳",
