   "platform": "x",
   "title": "What Indians need to realize right now is that since last year, it has become fundamentally impossible for China to continue exporting key t",
   "url": "https://x.com/961957192q83556/status/2113159293881172305",
   "snippet": "What Indians need to realize right now is that since last year, it has become fundamentally impossible for China to continue exporting key technologies, equipment, and raw materials to India without restrictions as it did in the past.\n\nPrior to this shift, China had never even considered imposing such export restrictions on India, because from Beijing's perspective, China's primary adversary is the United States. India was viewed as a potential ally, not a potential threat. As long as India maintained a friendly dialogue, it could reap unrestricted benefits from China’s economic and technological growth. What truly bewildered the Chinese people, however, was that India not only took the initiative to aggressively reduce its reliance on Chinese supply chains in search of alternatives, but also proudly beat the drums to advertise its potential threat to China—as if terrified that China might fail to notice.\n\nNow, India's self-fulfilling fears have become reality. Frankly, I have never witnessed a country act with such sheer foolishness",
   "body": "What Indians need to realize right now is that since last year, it has become fundamentally impossible for China to continue exporting key technologies, equipment, and raw materials to India without restrictions as it did in the past.\n\nPrior to this shift, China had never even considered imposing such export restrictions on India, because from Beijing's perspective, China's primary adversary is the United States. India was viewed as a potential ally, not a potential threat. As long as India maintained a friendly dialogue, it could reap unrestricted benefits from China’s economic and technological growth. What truly bewildered the Chinese people, however, was that India not only took the initiative to aggressively reduce its reliance on Chinese supply chains in search of alternatives, but also proudly beat the drums to advertise its potential threat to China—as if terrified that China might fail to notice.\n\nNow, India's self-fulfilling fears have become reality. Frankly, I have never witnessed a country act with such sheer foolishness",
   "bodyLevel": "post",
