   "title": "BREAKING: MALI, NIGER AND BURKINA FASO SHAMELESSLY CRAWL BACK BEGGING AFTER 18 MONTHS OUT OF ECOWAS Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger have resume",
   "url": "https://x.com/TheYorubaTimes/status/2112595533617410361",
   "snippet": "BREAKING: MALI, NIGER AND BURKINA FASO SHAMELESSLY CRAWL BACK BEGGING AFTER 18 MONTHS OUT OF ECOWAS\n\nBurkina Faso, Mali and Niger have resumed talks with ECOWAS more than 18 months after withdrawing from the regional bloc and forming the Alliance of Sahel States (AES).\n\nThe three military-led countries have now agreed with ECOWAS to establish joint working groups to develop a framework for cooperation, marking a dramatic shift after their decision to leave the organisation.\n\nTheir return to the negotiating table raises questions about the practical consequences of walking away from a regional bloc that connects West African economies through trade, movement and diplomatic cooperation. After months outside ECOWAS, the renewed talks suggest that regional realities may be harder to ignore than the political declarations that accompanied their withdrawal.",
   "body": "BREAKING: MALI, NIGER AND BURKINA FASO SHAMELESSLY CRAWL BACK BEGGING AFTER 18 MONTHS OUT OF ECOWAS\n\nBurkina Faso, Mali and Niger have resumed talks with ECOWAS more than 18 months after withdrawing from the regional bloc and forming the Alliance of Sahel States (AES).\n\nThe three military-led countries have now agreed with ECOWAS to establish joint working groups to develop a framework for cooperation, marking a dramatic shift after their decision to leave the organisation.\n\nTheir return to the negotiating table raises questions about the practical consequences of walking away from a regional bloc that connects West African economies through trade, movement and diplomatic cooperation. After months outside ECOWAS, the renewed talks suggest that regional realities may be harder to ignore than the political declarations that accompanied their withdrawal.",
